{
  "id": "UP08Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Lithotripsy (kidney stone)",
  "description": "Lithotripsy is a procedure to break up or remove kidney stones that are too large to pass on their own. Kidney stones are hard mineral deposits that can cause severe pain and block the flow of urine. Depending on the size and location of the stone, your doctor may use focused shock waves delivered from outside the body to shatter the stone into small pieces that you then pass in your urine, or, for larger stones, a minimally invasive surgery through a small incision in the back to remove the stone directly. The approach is chosen to fit your stone. Both are done with anesthesia so you are comfortable, and clearing the stone relieves pain and restores normal urine flow.",
